---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Shuffle as ShuffleIcon, Layers, BookOpen, Sparkles, Dices, Users, Scale, TrendingUp, Check, ArrowRight, MapPin, Gift } from 'lucide-astro';
import { getRegistrationData } from '../../lib/registration';

const { regStatus } = await getRegistrationData();
---

<Layout title="Shuffle League | Matt's Volleyball" description="Learn about the Wednesday shuffle league format at Matt's Volleyball. Teams are re-drafted weekly with the Level Up handicap system, plus free prize raffles every night.">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-ocean-600 to-ocean-800 text-white pt-20 md:pt-28">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h1 class="font-display font-black text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl mb-4">Shuffle League</h1>
      <p class="text-white/80 text-lg md:text-xl max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Social league first, volleyball second. Check in Wednesday night and get placed on balanced teams built from who's there.
      </p>
      <p class="text-white/50 text-sm mt-4">
        Powered by <a href="https://volleyballengine.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline hover:text-white/80 transition-colors">Volleyball Engine</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 80" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-full">
      <path d="M0 40C360 80 720 0 1080 40C1260 60 1380 50 1440 40V80H0V40Z" fill="#F7F6F3" />
    </svg>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">

      <!-- The Format -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="section-heading mb-6"><ShuffleIcon class="w-6 h-6 inline-block mr-2 -mt-1 text-ocean-500" />The Format</h2>
        <div class="text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            Everyone signs up as an individual. Each Wednesday, teams are generated from checked-in players so you'll play with and against different people over the season. All skill levels are welcome.
          </p>
          <p>
            The format is called "Level Up." Teams start each night at Level 1. Win a game and your team levels up, picking up a tougher handicap. The better you do, the harder it gets, which keeps matches competitive.
          </p>
          <p>
            Level 1 is intentionally social. Light icebreaker handicaps help new teammates learn names, communicate faster, and get comfortable playing together right away.
          </p>
          <p>
            Each season runs 6 regular-season nights over 6 weeks, plus 1 playoff night. Top teams advance to a single-elimination championship bracket with handicaps removed.
          </p>
          <p>
            Play runs for about 2 hours each night. Come late or leave early, no problem. On-time check-in helps us place you in the first wave of balanced teams.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- What to Expect -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="section-heading mb-6"><MapPin class="w-6 h-6 inline-block mr-2 -mt-1 text-ocean-500" />What to Expect When You Show Up</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="card p-6 flex gap-4 items-start">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-ocean-600 font-display font-bold shrink-0">1</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-ocean-600 mb-1">Check in by 6:30 PM</h3>
              <p class="text-ocean-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Show up and get marked present in the system. This is how we know who's playing and can build balanced teams. Checking in on time gives you the best chance to be in the first wave of games.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6 flex gap-4 items-start">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-ocean-600 font-display font-bold shrink-0">2</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-ocean-600 mb-1">Teams and schedules are generated around 6:40</h3>
              <p class="text-ocean-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Balanced teams are built fresh each week based on who showed up. You'll get your team assignment and a full schedule of pool play games - usually around 4, sometimes more depending on turnout.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6 flex gap-4 items-start">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-ocean-600 font-display font-bold shrink-0">3</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-ocean-600 mb-1">Play your games</h3>
              <p class="text-ocean-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Your team starts at Level 1. Win and you level up, gaining a handicap for your next game. Lose and you stay at your current level. Games are played to 21, rally scoring.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6 flex gap-4 items-start">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-ocean-600 font-display font-bold shrink-0">4</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-ocean-600 mb-1">Hang out</h3>
              <p class="text-ocean-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Grab a drink, meet new people, stick around after games. It's a social league - the volleyball is just the excuse to get together. Staying also keeps you in the running for the prize raffle.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Prize Raffle -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="section-heading mb-6"><Gift class="w-6 h-6 inline-block mr-2 -mt-1 text-ocean-500" />Prize Raffle</h2>
        <div class="text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            Every shuffle night includes a free prize raffle. There are no tickets to buy - checking in is your entry.
          </p>
          <p>
            Drawings happen between games throughout the night, with winners announced on the TV displays. To win you have to be checked in and still at the courts, so stick around. Each player can win once per night, which spreads the prizes around.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- The Five Levels -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="section-heading mb-8"><Layers class="w-6 h-6 inline-block mr-2 -mt-1 text-ocean-500" />Sample Restrictions by Level</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-sand-300">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
              <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-sand-300 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-white font-display font-bold">1</span>
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-xl text-ocean-600">Level 1: Standard Play</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed">Social and silly handicaps to break the ice fast. Examples: <em>tell your worst joke before serving (if anyone laughs, you earn a point)</em> or <em>offer an opponent unsolicited coaching advice before each rotation's first serve</em>.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-sand-400">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
              <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-sand-400 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-white font-display font-bold">2</span>
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-xl text-ocean-600">Level 2: Mild Restrictions</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed">Light gameplay restrictions. Examples: <em>all sets must be bump sets</em> or <em>serve backwards or with your eyes closed</em>.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-coral-400">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
              <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-coral-400 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-white font-display font-bold">3</span>
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-xl text-ocean-600">Level 3: Moderate Restrictions</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed">Tighter gameplay restrictions. Examples: <em>only female players can attack</em> or <em>the opposing team designates your strongest hitter, who must play defense the entire game</em>.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-coral-500">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
              <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-coral-500 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-white font-display font-bold">4</span>
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-xl text-ocean-600">Level 4: Tough Restrictions</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed">Tough restrictions that limit your best weapons. Examples: <em>all serves must be underhand</em>, <em>no blocking allowed</em>, or <em>serve with your non-dominant hand</em>.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-ocean-600">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
              <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-600 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-white font-display font-bold">5</span>
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-xl text-ocean-600">Level 5: Extreme Restrictions</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed">Extreme restrictions that flip how volleyball works. Examples: <em>no one on your team is allowed to jump</em> or <em>only two touches to get the ball back over</em>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ocean-600/70 text-sm mt-4 italic">These are examples. Handicaps rotate weekly to keep things fresh.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Baseline Rules -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="section-heading mb-6"><BookOpen class="w-6 h-6 inline-block mr-2 -mt-1 text-ocean-500" />Baseline Rules (All Levels)</h2>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md p-6 md:p-8">
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            {[
              'No net touching or interference',
              'No lifts or hand setting over the net',
              'No open-handed tips',
              "Server's foot cannot cross end line",
              'Players call violations honestly',
              'Disputes resolved by replaying points',
            ].map((rule) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-ocean-700">
                <Check class="w-5 h-5 text-ocean-600 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
                {rule}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Why This Format Works -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="section-heading mb-6"><Sparkles class="w-6 h-6 inline-block mr-2 -mt-1 text-ocean-500" />Why This Format Works</h2>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="card p-6">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <Dices class="w-5 h-5 text-ocean-500" />
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-ocean-600">Variety</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-ocean-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Random handicaps and rotating teammates keep every week fresh and unpredictable.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <Users class="w-5 h-5 text-ocean-500" />
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-ocean-600">Social</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-ocean-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Prevents cliques. You'll play with and against everyone by the end of the season. Level 1 social handicaps help break the ice fast.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <Scale class="w-5 h-5 text-ocean-500" />
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-ocean-600">Self-Balancing</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-ocean-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Stronger teams are handicapped as they win, and teams are generated from check-ins to keep games balanced and competitive.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <TrendingUp class="w-5 h-5 text-ocean-500" />
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-ocean-600">Skill Building</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-ocean-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Tests fundamental skills when standard techniques become unavailable.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-sand-200">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-4">
        Ready to shuffle?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-ocean-600/80 text-lg mb-8">
        {regStatus === 'open'
          ? 'Join Wednesday Shuffle for balanced games, rotating teammates, and a great social night.'
          : 'Check out Wednesday Shuffle for balanced games, rotating teammates, and a great social night.'}
      </p>
      {regStatus === 'open' ? (
        <a
          href="https://app.teamlinkt.com/register/find/mattsvolleyball"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="btn-primary inline-flex items-center gap-2"
        >
          Register Now
          <ArrowRight class="w-4 h-4" />
        </a>
      ) : (
        <a href="/leagues/" class="btn-primary inline-flex items-center gap-2">
          View Leagues
          <ArrowRight class="w-4 h-4" />
        </a>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
